.dgo-shell-grid{height:calc(100vh - 26px);min-height:0}
/* Surface context (Phase 5a). The sidebar is an inverse surface in every theme, so the
   page-level foreground semantics do not describe it. base.css paints `strong, b` with
   --dgo-color-fg-strong, which is #1B1A1A in light and #000000 in hc, so the brand lockup and
   the signed-in identity rendered dark-on-dark: measured 1.09:1 and 1.32:1 on all 24 routes.
   Re-binding the three foreground semantics on the surface itself fixes every descendant that
   reads them — including ones added later — instead of patching each rule.

   `background` is no longer declared here: components.css already gives .dgo-sidebar
   `background: var(--dgo-sidebar-bg)`, which the theme files re-bind (#022819 light,
   #081109 dark, #000000 hc). This rule was overriding it with the raw --dgo-green-900
   primitive from the last layer, which is why neither `dark` nor `hc` reached the sidebar. */
